# Practical 5 – Time Table Using One-Way Data Binding

## Aim

To create an Angular application to display a timetable using one-way data binding.

## Objective

To understand how one-way data binding is used in Angular to display data from the TypeScript component on the HTML page.

## 1. app.ts

import { Component, signal } from '@angular/core';
import { RouterOutlet } from '@angular/router';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  imports: [RouterOutlet],
  templateUrl: './app.html',
  styleUrl: './app.css'
})
export class App {
   day = 'Monday';
   subject = 'Angular';
   time = '10:00 AM - 11:00 AM';
}

